  {
    "episode_id": 84248,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84248.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, the most disappointing thing is that they don't want to get anything done. You know, and even when I can find places where we agree with, you know, with them, they're not willing to really work on anything. You know, Matt Kate, who really has you know, bow down to Donald Trump and does whatever Trump asks him to do. He has some opinions that we could, you know, conceivably work together with him on, for example, decriminalizing marijuana because he's something of a libertine about that. And so we obviously think that the war on drugs is a failure and we should stop ruining young people's lives by getting them a criminal record that makes it impossible for them to find work and get on with their lives and so on. But they just won't do anything. And they don't want anything to succeed. And I don't think that the Rules Committee has sent out a bill that has passed in the House in more than eight or nine months. Unless the Democrats are going to build them out, like the way we build out the speaker on the various budget deals. But I don't think they can't agree on anything amongst themselves much less agree with us.",
