    "turn_idx": 74,
    "turn_text": "First of all, thank you for lobbying me and pushing me on this and opening my eyes to it. That's what gave me the idea to do the press act. But it establishes a journalistic privilege for reporters so that they are not being subpoenaed for their confidential sources. They're not forced to give up their sources unless there's a terrorist attack going on or a matter of national security. But to me, this is just the natural logic of the freedom of the press under the First Amendment. Will it pass the Senate? Well, it passed the House and we're hopeful it passed the Senate. I think we've got some good momentum there. So it would be a miracle in this Congress because it really is a do-nothing Congress if we were able to get it through. But my fingers are crossed. I'm knocking on wood and I hope everybody can rally around the Constitution and the freedom of the press. The press is not The people's worst enemy is the last president said the press is the people's best friend Yeah, and we need the press and we'll have come back another time to talk about about corporate concentration and deconcentrating Monopoly",
